From: Jonas Karlsson <jonas.karlsson@qt.io>
Subject: [PATCH] PhysX: Leave the mutex priority ceiling out for emscripten

Emscripten is PX_LINUX to PhysX, so the mutex constructor calls
pthread_mutexattr_setprioceiling(). Its musl has no such function, and
emscripten only defines one in the threaded pthread library, where it
does nothing but return EPERM. A build without pthreads links the stub
library instead, which has no definition, so every application linking
PhysX failed with an undefined symbol for it.

Skip the call for emscripten altogether; it cannot set a ceiling with or
without threads. pthread_mutexattr_setprotocol() comes from musl itself,
which the single threaded libc includes, so it stays.
---
 src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/foundation/unix/FdUnixMutex.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/foundation/unix/FdUnixMutex.cpp b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/foundation/unix/FdUnixMutex.cpp
--- a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/foundation/unix/FdUnixMutex.cpp
+++ b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/foundation/unix/FdUnixMutex.cpp
@@ -71,8 +71,9 @@ PxMutexImpl::PxMutexImpl()
 #if PX_LINUX && !defined(__BIONIC__)
 	pthread_mutexattr_setprotocol(&attr, gMutexProtocol);
 #endif
-// the OHOS SDK declares no pthread_mutexattr_setprioceiling()
-#if PX_LINUX && !defined(__BIONIC__) && !defined(__OHOS__)
+// the OHOS SDK declares no pthread_mutexattr_setprioceiling(), and emscripten
+// only defines it when building with pthreads
+#if PX_LINUX && !defined(__BIONIC__) && !defined(__OHOS__) && !defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
 	pthread_mutexattr_setprioceiling(&attr, 0);
 #endif
 	pthread_mutex_init(&getMutex(this)->lock, &attr);
